    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114-a3">

                <pb facs="0207" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg861"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    237.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lafragua to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 29,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to remit inclosed to your
                    excellency copies of five communications relative to the unfortunate affair
                    which happened in Acapulco on the night of the 26th of the present month, and to
                    which your excellency refers in your notes of the 27th and 28th of the same
                    month.</p>
                <p>By said communications your excellency will see that there have been ordered and
                    there are being ordered the appropriate measures, by this department and by the
                    departments of justice, interior; (<hi rendition="#italic">gobernacion</hi>,)
                    and war, to the end that peace and order may be insured in that locality, that
                    religious liberty of the interested parties may be guaranteed, and the
                    apprehension and punishment of those who may be found guilty may be secured.</p>
                <p>I improve this opportunity to renew to your excellency the assurances of my very
                    distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. M. LAFRAGUA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To his Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            the United States of America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
